## Theme Subscription Utility Implementation Complete

### Location
- **Utility File:** `src/public/theme-subscription.js`
- **TypeScript Definitions:** `src/types/theme-subscription.d.ts`
- **Documentation:** `docs/theme-subscription-utility.md`
- **Test File:** `test-theme-subscription.html`

### API Overview
The utility provides a clean, type-safe API for platform frame components to subscribe to theme changes:

```javascript
// Subscribe to theme changes
const subscriberId = ThemeSubscription.subscribe((theme) => {
  console.log('Theme changed to:', theme);
  // Update component
});

// Unsubscribe
ThemeSubscription.unsubscribe(subscriberId);

// Get current theme
const currentTheme = ThemeSubscription.getCurrentTheme();

// Platform frame convenience method
const unsubscribe = ThemeSubscription.subscribePlatformFrame('twitter', 'frame-id');
```

### Features
- ✅ Subscribe/Unsubscribe API with callbacks
- ✅ Current theme access (`getCurrentTheme()`)
- ✅ Platform frame integration (`applyThemeToFrame`, `subscribePlatformFrame`)
- ✅ Full TypeScript type definitions
- ✅ Works with existing frames-theme.js system
- ✅ Automatic theme change detection via MutationObserver
- ✅ Error handling for subscriber callbacks
- ✅ Tested and verified working

### Usage in Platform Frame Components
```typescript
class TwitterFrame implements BasePlatformFrame {
  private unsubscribe: (() => void) | null = null;

  mount() {
    this.unsubscribe = window.ThemeSubscription.subscribePlatformFrame(
      'twitter',
      this.frameId
    );
  }

  unmount() {
    if (this.unsubscribe) {
      this.unsubscribe();
    }
  }
}
```

### Integration Status
The utility is ready for integration into the 7 platform frame components:
- facebook-frame.ts
- instagram-frame.ts  
- linkedin-frame.ts
- reddit-frame.ts
- tiktok-frame.ts
- twitter-frame.ts
- youtube-frame.ts

Each component can now use `ThemeSubscription.subscribePlatformFrame()` or the lower-level `subscribe()` API to receive theme changes without page reload.
